## 24. MOST PRECISE DISTINCTION

Do not confuse:

```csharp
Task.WhenAll(tasks);
```

with:

```csharp
await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
```

### Task.WhenAll()

Creates/returns a Task representing:

```text
"All supplied Tasks have completed."
```

### await

Asynchronously waits for that Task.

Therefore:

```csharp
await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
```

is really two concepts combined:

```text
Task.WhenAll(tasks)
        |
        v
   Combined Task
        |
        v
      await
        |
        v
Asynchronously wait
```

This distinction is extremely useful in interviews.

